###      BASIC COMMANDS OF K8's     ###

>                           <<<<<<<PODS>>>>>>>

>>>>>>> create pod <<<<<<<

    1. create a pod :- kubectl run nginx --image=nginx
    2. create with a specific name :- kubectl run my-pod --image=nginx

>>>>>>>> check pod <<<<<<

    3. check pods :- kubectl get pods
    4. check pods more details :- kubectl get pods -o wide
    5. watch pod status :- kubectl get pods -w
    6. check all namespace :- kubectl get pods -A

    7. describe a pod :- kubectl describe pod nginx
     
    8. get pod YAML :- kubectl get pod nginx -o yaml
    9. get pod JSON :- kubectl get pod nginx -o json

>>>>>>>> Check Pod Logs <<<<<<<<<

    10. check pod logs :- kubectl logs (pod-name) -n (namespace)
    11. follow live logs :- kubectl logs -f (pod-name) -n (namespace)
    12. if the pods have multiple container :- kubectl logs nginx -c container-name
    
>>>>>>>>>    execute commands inside pods <<<<<<<<<
    
    13. open shell :- kubectl exec -it (pod-name) -n (namespace) -- /bin/bash/
    14. open shell if bash not available :- kubectl exec -it (pod-name) -n (namespace) -- /bin/sh/
    15. run a single command :- kubectl exec (pod-name) -n (namespace) --ls

>>>>>>>>> delete pods <<<<<<<<<
    
    16. delete single pod :- kubectl delete pod (podname) -n (namespace)
    17. delete multiple pod :- kubectl delete pod pod1 pod2 -n (namespace)
    18. delete all pods :- kubectl delete pods --all -n (namespace)

>>>>>>>>> create pod from YAML <<<<<<<<<

    19. create pod :- kubectl apply -f pod.yaml
    20. check pod :- kubectl get pods
    21. delete pod :- kubectl delete -f pod.yaml

>   22. get pod IP :- kubectl get pod -o wide

    